    {
      "id": "claim_10a3c5c1413740b791e6bec62399cb59",
      "statement": "logSet() re-authenticates via requireUser(), inserts into set_log using an idempotency_key so a unique-constraint conflict (23505) returns the existing row instead of erroring, computes e1rm at write time, then calls recomputeAndUpsertStat() to rebuild user_exercise_stat; if that rebuild throws, the function still returns the successful set write with a recomputeWarning instead of failing the write.",
      "evidence": [
